 "poem": "And May is all sweet the morning,\nIs all sweet the night before,\nPanting with faith and baring our\nSleeves bare to the world's power.\nNow the deep-breathed East hath bid us, bidding,\nAs though we went not by way of heaven,\nBidding us of our dearest desire,\nCome forth as one who comes too early. For\nThe stars are low to reach our\nEyes and hearts, but the hour\nOf dawn on them will be great; for our\nSmiles are too many; ours",
